{
  "dom_id": "step-54187",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Identifying the Equation of a Proportional Relationship",
  "problem": "Beatrice needs to clean the garage. So, to motivate herself, she allows herself $10$ minutes of video game time for every $25$ minutes she spends cleaning.\n\nThere is a proportional relationship between the time $x$ (in minutes) Beatrice spends cleaning the garage and the time $y$ (in minutes) she plays video games. What equation represents the relationship between $x$ and $y?$",
  "worked_solution": "Every proportional relationship takes the form $y=kx,$ where $k$ is the constant of proportionality.\n\nWe are told that for every $x=25$ minutes Beatrice spends cleaning, she will play $y=10$ minutes of video games.\n\nWe can find the constant of proportionality by computing the ratio of the $y$-value to the $x$-value, as follows:\n\n$$\nk = \\dfrac{y}{x} = \\dfrac{10}{25} = \\dfrac{10 \\div 5}{25 \\div 5} = \\dfrac{2}{5}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation is\n\n$$\ny = \\dfrac{2}{5} x.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
